  "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{X}={2.4,3.8,15.3}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{Y}={2,7.1,19.2},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{X\\cap Y}?$",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{X\\cap Y}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{X}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{Y}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{X\\cap Y} & =\\overset{\u2015}{X}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{Y} \\\\  & ={2.4,3.8,15.3}\\cup {2,7.1,19.2} \\\\  & ={2,2.4,3.8,7.1,15.3,19.2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
